node_modules/
# Ignore every .env sibling and un-ignore only the tracked template. The files
# at risk (.env.bak-20260724, .env.bak-concierge-20260806-021701, editor .env~,
# sed -i.bak output) all carry API_KEY in plaintext and are written by tooling
# OUTSIDE this repo, so their naming surface cannot be enumerated from in here —
# a prefix match is the only form that closes rather than chases.
# Deliberately swallows .envrc too: direnv configs commonly hold secrets, and
# silently untracking one is a far cheaper mistake than committing it. Anything
# here that genuinely belongs in git needs an explicit `git add -f`.
.env*
!.env.example
.machine_config_hash
.reporting-state.json
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
